\section{Proposed study}
Re-run GTS and Graph WaveNet on one explicitly versioned METR-LA dataset. Use one chronological train/validation/test split and one normalization implementation. Evaluate the same 15-, 30-, and 60-minute horizons separately, and distinguish these from averages over horizons. Define exactly which zero or missing targets are masked. Use the corrected metric implementation and record the code commit. Repeat training with shared seeds and report mean and standard deviation, with no selection of only the best run. Keep cited baseline values separate from independently reproduced results. These are proposed controls; no model-training experiment has been conducted.
\subsection{Controls required by the evidence}
\begin{itemize}
\item Compute every metric with one stated definition, including how zero or missing targets are masked; report masked and unmasked values when baselines differ.
\item Report each forecast horizon separately (for example 15, 30, and 60 minutes) and report the average over horizons as a separate row; never compare one with the other.
\end{itemize}
